# Calibration test templates

## Canonical source

`tester-v1/calibration-tests/` is the only source for shared probe YAML. The create-model-configs skill scaffolds from `tester-v1/templates/`, never from live model dirs.

**In calibration-tests:** global probes for calibration and run-test (`calibration-footprint`, `calibration-ctx-probe`, `hello-world-baseline`, plus any future promoted probes). Each variant has `client.yaml` and a thin `server.yaml` (ctx-size override only).

**Not in calibration-tests:** per-model sandbox prompts. Add those under `models/{model}/sandbox/client.yaml` (optional `sandbox/server.yaml` override) and run with `--variant sandbox`.

## Promote / demote

- **Promote:** add `{variant}/server.yaml` (ctx override) and `client.yaml` under `calibration-tests/`, then register the variant in `tester-v1/src/calibration.py` (today hardcoded to the three names above). Do not copy probe YAML into live model dirs; see `calibration-tests-sync.mdc`.
- **Demote:** remove from `calibration-tests/` only; live copies may stay.

**Default edits:** change shared behavior in `calibration-tests/`. Ad-hoc tweaks stay in that model's `sandbox/` dir and are not copied to `calibration-tests/` unless promoted.

When `calibration-tests/` changes, follow `calibration-tests-sync.mdc`.

## How calibration uses calibration-tests

`tester_v1_calibrate.py` validates `calibration-tests/{variant}/`, then runs probes in-process with:

- base load profile from `models/{model}/server.yaml`
- probe server/client from `calibration-tests/{variant}/` (thin server.yaml merged on top of model server.yaml)
- model path from `models/{model}/model.yaml`

## Do not run on calibration-tests

Never pass `tester-v1/calibration-tests/` (or a variant under it) to `tester_v1_run_test.py`. Pass `models/{model}/` and use `--variant` to select a shared probe or local sandbox.
